==Trivia== 
*The Ice Spirit's Evolution is tied with the [[Skeletons/Evolution|Skeletons]] for the cheapest [[Card Evolution|Evolution]] to be placed, costing 3 [[Elixir]] (excluding Elixir from using other [[cards]]).
*The Ice Spirit's Evolution is 1 of 3 evolved [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] to die as part of its attack, the other being the [[Wall Breakers/Evolution|Wall Breakers]], and Runners.
*In the French, Italian, Portuguese, Malaysian, and Finnish language settings of the game, the Ice Spirit's name translates to "Spirit of Ice". In the Persian language settings of the game, the Ice Spirit's name translates to "Ice Soul".
*The Ice Spirit's Evolution is 1 of 5 cards that has had its Cycles required changed, the others being [[Bomber/Evolution|Bomber]], Skeletons, [[Lumberjack/Evolution|Lumberjack]], and [[Baby Dragon/Evolution|Baby Dragon]].
*The Ice Spirit’s gender is confirmed to be male, as in the balance changes in the [[Version History#April%202022%20Update%20(4/4/2022)|April 2022 Update]] it states, "''We want to provide more distinct use for the Ice Spirit compared to his counterparts the Electro Spirit.''"
*The Ice Spirit's Evolution is 1 of 3 evolved cards without the diamond evolution symbol anywhere on their card render, the others being [[Bats/Evolution|Bats]] and Giant Snowball.
*In [[Touchdown]], if an Ice Spirit jumps into the enemy end zone as it attacks, it does not count as a point. This is because a jumping spirit no longer counts as a troop; it becomes similar to a projectile.
*The Ice Spirit's Evolution is the subject of 2 [[Emotes]].
*The Ice Spirit is the only spirit - among [[Fire Spirit]], [[Electro Spirit]] and [[Heal Spirit]] - to have an evolution.

